+      a COUNT-matched random elimination operator. A count-matched random control is WEAK: it ignores
+      the score distribution. The sharper question: does the ensemble preferentially SPARE correct
+      candidates beyond what a control with the SAME score-distribution (stratified/score-matched
+      random elimination) would, with a bootstrap CI on the margin so we know if 0.010 is signal or noise?
